<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Foreground alpha of the *folder* page's post-commit back exit.

     This resource exists only for the album grid -> home return. The settings, theme
     and custom-photo-profile pages keep the shared oxygen_classic_page_back_alpha curve.

     Why the folder page needs its own curve
     =======================================
     With OxygenClassicPageBackWindow the Shell selects
     CustomCrossActivityBackAnimation, which freezes the closing rect at the release
     position and keeps the entering parent on a full-screen base rect with alpha pinned
     to 1. The parent is therefore already fully composed underneath, so every frame of
     foreground alpha is a literal cross-dissolve of two grids. The previous curve ended
     that dissolve at 35% of a 450 ms clock and then held alpha 0 for the remaining
     ~293 ms, i.e. the page vanished while the clock kept running and the window was
     removed afterwards. That is the "suddenly switches to the full home page" reading.

     Shape of this curve (y = fade fraction, alpha = 1 - y)
     ======================================================
     - y grows slowly at first (~0.04 by 10%), so the release frame does not lose
       opacity and the first part of the exit is motion, not dissolve;
     - the steepest part sits between 35% and 60%, where the paired slide curve is
       moving fastest, so the dissolve happens while the page is visibly leaving;
     - y reaches 1 only at progress 1, on the same frame the travel completes. There is
       no invisible tail and no hard cut: the last visible frame precedes the window
       removal by one frame.
     Full-clock children keep the Shell's unclamped 0..1 progress mapping exact at both
     ends (alpha 1 at 0, alpha 0 at 1).

     PathInterpolator contract: the path starts at (0,0), ends at (1,1) and x is
     strictly increasing (0.18 -> 0.33 -> 0.55 -> 0.74 -> 0.90 -> 1). -->
<pathInterpolator xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:pathData="M0,0 C0.18,0.03 0.33,0.30 0.55,0.72 C0.74,0.92 0.90,0.99 1,1" />
